   "text": "This is a symmetric dimer: two identical bicyclic pyrrolidine-thiazepinone cores, each carrying an N-methyl-L-alanyl amide, joined through two aminoindanol units by a but-2-yne-1,4-diyl diether linker.\n\n**Left half, fragment by fragment**\n- N-Methylalanine: the \u03b1-carbon has N to the left, C=O to the right and a hashed methyl. This works out as S (L-Ala), written `CN[C@@H](C)C(=O)N\u2026`.\n- Thiazepinone ring: S, CH2, CH2, CH(NH-acyl), C(=O), N and the ring-fusion CH (hashed H) form the seven-membered ring. The CH(NH) carbon is S and the ring-fusion CH next to S is S.\n- Pyrrolidine ring: the N, the CH bearing the amide (wedged), a CMe2, a CH2 and the ring-fusion CH. The amide-bearing carbon is S.\n- Indane: C1 bears the NH (hashed) and C2 bears the O (hashed). This works out as C1 S and C2 R.\n- Linker: the indane O\u2013CH2\u2013C\u2261C\u2013CH2\u2013O connects to the second indane.\n\n**Right half**\nThe right half is the same unit rotated by 180\u00b0, so it has the same absolute configuration. I rewrote its chirality tags for the reversed atom order by counting permutations of the neighbour lists.\n\nSMILES: CN[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@H]1CCS[C@H]2CC(C)(C)[C@@H](C(=O)N[C@H]3c4ccccc4C[C@H]3OCC#CCO[C@@H]3Cc4ccccc4[C@@H]3NC(=O)[C@@H]5C(C)(C)C[C@@H]6SCC[C@H](NC(=O)[C@H](C)NC)C(=O)N56)N2C1=O"
